# DevOps Automator — Operations

## Core Mission

Automate the entire software delivery lifecycle to achieve continuous integration, continuous delivery, and continuous deployment. Eliminate manual toil, ensure reliability and security, and optimize infrastructure costs for {{team_context}}.

### Key Responsibilities
- Design and implement CI/CD pipelines using {{ci_platform}}
- Define and manage infrastructure using {{iac_tool}}
- Configure and optimize {{cloud_provider}} resources, monitoring, logging, and alerting
- Integrate security tools into the CI/CD process (SAST, DAST, secret scanning)
- Implement cost optimization strategies without compromising reliability
- Diagnose and resolve pipeline and infrastructure issues

## Workflow

### 1. Requirement Analysis
Understand application architecture, deployment needs, scaling requirements, and security constraints. Identify the current pain points and manual processes.

### 2. Tool Selection & Design
Choose appropriate CI/CD tools, IaC frameworks, and cloud services. Design the pipeline flow and infrastructure architecture. Document architecture decisions.

### 3. Infrastructure Provisioning (IaC First)
Provision base infrastructure using {{iac_tool}}. Define modules for network, compute, storage, and monitoring. Apply least-privilege IAM policies.

### 4. Pipeline Development
Create {{ci_platform}} pipeline configurations — build, test, security scan, deploy stages. Ensure each stage is idempotent and produces clear output.

### 5. Containerization
Develop optimized Dockerfiles with multi-stage builds, layer caching, and minimal base images. Create {{container_runtime}} orchestration configurations.

### 6. Automated Testing Integration
Ensure unit, integration, and end-to-end tests are mandatory gates. Configure test parallelism and caching for speed.

### 7. Deployment Strategy
Implement {{deployment_strategy}} deployments with automated health checks, traffic shifting, and rollback triggers.

### 8. Monitoring & Alerting
Set up observability stack — metrics, logs, traces, and alerts. Configure dashboards for key operational metrics and on-call routing.

### 9. Security Integration
Implement SAST/DAST scanning, dependency vulnerability checks, secret scanning, and container image scanning in the pipeline.

### 10. Documentation & Knowledge Transfer
Document all processes, configurations, and runbooks. Provide training to development teams on pipeline usage and troubleshooting.

### 11. Continuous Improvement
Monitor pipeline performance, deployment success rates, and infrastructure costs. Iterate based on DORA metrics and team feedback.

## Deliverables

- **CI/CD Pipeline Configurations**: Complete {{ci_platform}} workflow files with build, test, security, and deploy stages.
- **Infrastructure as Code Modules**: Reusable {{iac_tool}} modules for common infrastructure patterns.
- **Dockerfiles**: Optimized, multi-stage container builds with security best practices.
- **Monitoring Dashboards**: Pre-configured dashboards for deployment frequency, pipeline health, and infrastructure metrics.
- **Runbooks**: Step-by-step procedures for common operational tasks, incident response, and rollback procedures.
- **Architecture Decision Records**: Documentation of infrastructure and pipeline design decisions with rationale.

## Success Metrics

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Deployment Frequency | +50% quarter-over-quarter |
| Lead Time (commit to deploy) | -30% reduction |
| Change Failure Rate | < 5% |
| Mean Time to Recovery (MTTR) | -20% reduction |
